# Overlay themes

Full contract: [`docs/THEMES.md`](../../docs/THEMES.md). A theme is the **look** of the
overlay surface (glass, glow, pulse) plus preferred fonts. It is not layout and not the
settings chrome.

## Folder shape

`themes/<id>/` holds `theme.json`, `theme.css`, and `theme.js` (only if it has motion).

- Scope every selector to `[data-theme="<id>"]`. **Never style `#settings-menu`** — the
  panel stays as specified in [`docs/Control_UI.md`](../../docs/Control_UI.md).
- Style the glass surface via `.theme-panel` (the banner box, not the page). Page
  background stays `transparent`.

## Keep the catalog in sync

`theme.json` and the `SeshThemes.catalog` entry registered in `theme.js` must carry the
same `id`, `name`, `description`, `preferredDisplay`, and `preferredRegular`. Apps read
the catalog; the JSON is metadata for meat bags and tooling. Preferred faces must exist
in the typography catalog ([`docs/TYPOGRAPHY.md`](../../docs/TYPOGRAPHY.md)).

## Effect lifecycle

`SeshThemes.effects[id].start(el)` / `.stop(el)`. One panel gets one animation runner —
switching themes repeatedly must not multiply clanker heartbeats.

```js
function start(panelEl) {
  if (!panelEl) return;
  stop(panelEl);                     // cancel any existing runner for this element
  /* ... requestAnimationFrame loop, tracked in a WeakMap ... */
}

function stop(panelEl) {
  /* cancelAnimationFrame + drop the runner, then: */
  panelEl.style.removeProperty('--theme-text-shadow');  // strip inline theme props
  panelEl.style.removeProperty('text-shadow');          // so the next theme starts clean
}
```

Glass themes write `--theme-text-shadow` so child text pulses.

## Adding or changing a theme

Link the CSS/JS from each consuming app, persist the choice as URL param `theme` (live
update contract applies), and test switching themes back and forth — including that
preferred fonts apply when font params are absent and when the theme select changes.
